{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"The policy for every mutating action, and — in the ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"actions","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" module (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"actions.rs","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" plus ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"actions/","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":") — the only code in rc-git that performs one. Branch and tag management go through here; so does everything that comes later.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Every entry point calls ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"authorize","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (actions.rs), which runs ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Policy::authorize","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":": the policy evaluates the ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Action","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" itself and returns a ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Confirmation","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" for an ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Allow","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", through ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Challenge::verify","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" for a ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Confirm","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", or the refusal. Every write is a method on ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"actions/write.rs","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"'s ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Writer","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", built only by ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Writer::new(repo, &confirmation)","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", so the type system forces a verified challenge, and the typed phrase only where the policy names one. A confirm with no phrase verifies for any input: its button lives in the front end (the GUI's confirm step, the CLI's ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"--yes","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"). ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Challenge","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" and ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Confirmation","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" have fields private to ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"policy.rs","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"; nothing else in the crate can build either one.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"The front end renders decisions; it never classifies an action itself and never offers a one-click path around a challenge. The FFI passes the user's typed input through; the verification lives here.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
